1. She owns a 2-meter goose plush that she hugs. (Verbatim: "I'm gonna go hug my 2 meter goose plush.")
2. She refers to her audience as "my brothers and sisters and goose," indicating a recurring thematic bond with geese. (Verbatim: "Thank you, my brothers and sisters and goose")
3. She created a humorous, uncensored version of a bedtime book titled *Go the F to Sleep*. (Verbatim: "The giant pangolins of Madagascar are snoozing as I lie here and openly weep. Sure, fine, whatever, I'll bring you some milk. Who the eff cares you're not going to sleep?")
4. She plans to release a free voice pack featuring her reading of *Go the F to Sleep* once it arrives. (Verbatim: "you're going to get the uncensored full version as a free voice pack as soon as the book arrives and I can read the rest.")
5. She has a running joke or ritual involving “Remy” spoiling things, suggesting an inside joke or lore element. (Verbatim: "Remy! Why are you spoiling? I'm already spoiled!")
6. She uses a fictional or satirical religious phrase referencing “O banana” and “eternal zatsu,” indicating absurdist or comedic lore. (Verbatim: "Create a clean heart within me, O banana, and purify me of all mortal possessions. Renew a right spirit within me, that I may dwell with the goose in eternal zatsu. Amen.")
7. She has a plush named Skittles that was “eaten” (likely part of a joke or roleplay). (Verbatim: "Skittles, sorry. I think yours got eaten. It got nom-nomed.")
8. She frequently expresses deep emotional gratitude toward her audience, wishing English had a stronger word than “thank you.” (Verbatim: "I wish- I wish the English language had a better word for 'thank you'. Like a stronger 'thank you'.")
9. She avoids saying “bye-bye” and instead uses “see you later” as a farewell, treating “bye-byes” as something negative. (Verbatim: "it's not a bye-bye, okay? It's not a bye-bye, because bye-byes suck, okay?")
10. She ends her streams with a dramatic “big zoom in” where her face fills the screen, declaring “BOOM! And then BOOM!” (Verbatim: "Time for the big zoom in. This is how I finish my streams for anyone new. We go BOOM! And then BOOM!") [end of text]



